ecorative SVG and output text are hidden via `aria-hidden=\"true\"`"],[76,"The dismiss button defaults to `aria-label=\"Close\"`. Override it via `ariaLabels={{ close: '...' }}` to provide more specific context for screen readers (e.g. `\"Dismiss payment warning\"`). This is especially useful when multiple alerts are visible at the same time."],[575,"The drop zone renders a visually hidden `<button>` inside the container. Assistive technology discovers and announces this button as an interactive element — activating it opens the native file picker without a pointer."],[1251,"The examples include their CSS in `<style>` blocks so the complete code is visible. Applications can\nplace those rules in their own stylesheets. Layout props such as `columns` and `gap` write inline styles,\nwhich beat stylesheet rules. When your CSS changes a property across a query, set it in CSS for every\nwidth and leave the prop unset."],[1527,"The eyebrow is decorative in most designs. If it carries meaning, make sure the title still\nreads sensibly on its own, since screen reader users often navigate by heading."],[1194,"The final marker is missing"],[685,"The following methods are exported from `@godaddy/antares` for custom icon management:"],[678,"The Icon component uses Bento's slot system with the following component hierarchy and available slot override points:"],[953,"The info trigger button uses `aria-label=\"More information\"` to describe its purpose."],[955,"The info trigger has a minimum touch target of 44×44px, achieved via a CSS pseudo-element, to meet WCAG 2.5.5."],[1381,"The interactive switch control exposes data attributes for styling different states:"],[409,"The menu trigger does not look like a Chip"],[939,"The MetricsLockup component displays a single metric with an optional title, info tooltip, trend indicator, and description."],[961,"The Modal component presents a dialog window over the page that focuses the user's attention on a single task or piece of information."],[972,"The modal is a `SizeProvider`. It opens at the size of the scope around its trigger, even though it renders in a portal, and `size` overrides that."],[1321,"The nearest scope wins, and nested scopes replace the size rather than compounding it."],[1026,"The Popover component is an overlay element positioned relative to a trigger element."],[1198,"The range configuration is invalid"],[407,"The remove action does not update the UI"],[825,"The spacing props use semantic t-shirt sizes for padding, gap, and other spacing properties:"],[1525,"The title carries the heading semantics. Choose `level` so the page outline stays correct\nrather than to achieve a size."],[1608,"The Tooltip component displays a description of an element on hover or focus."],[1630,"The tooltip uses `role=\"tooltip\"` and is associated with its focusable element via `aria-describedby`"],[954,"The tooltip uses `role=\"tooltip\"` and is associated with the info trigger via `aria-describedby`."],[1383,"The track and thumb read from Antares curated tokens, falling back to legacy `--ux-*` custom properties:"],[1196,"The value or endpoint labels are blank"],[689,"These are re-exports of the underlying Bento Icon system methods. For complete API documentation, advanced usage patterns, and implementation details, see the `@bento/icon` and `@bento/svg-parser` package documentation."],[1255,"These components follow `--antares-size`:"],[15,"This also works with autocomplete in IDEs and LLMs, so you can import from the root package and let your editor/agent suggest the available components."],[721,"This approach works well for SSR and small numbers of icons, but can lead to DOM bloat when the same icon appears many times."],[1104,"Timeline (past / current / future) derived from a single `currentStep` prop"],[1107,"Title truncation and RTL support"],[416,"Toggle Chips for selecting multiple peer filters"],[1551,"ToggleButton"],[1574,"ToggleButton"],[1573,"ToggleButtonGroup"],[1371,"Toggles on click or