"` to arrange them in a row."],[1061,"Use `Pressable` when an existing visual component or layout surface needs press behavior while keeping its own DOM element, layout, and styles. The child must be a single element that forwards its ref and accepts the DOM, ARIA, and event props supplied by React Aria."],[1435,"Use `TabList`'s `containerProps` to customize the outer tab list shell, such as increasing its width."],[125,"Use `target=\"_blank\"` to open a link in a new tab without an icon. `isExternal` adds an icon and defaults\nto `target=\"_blank\"` and `rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`; explicit `target` and `rel` override those defaults.\nYou can also compose an `Icon` as a child independently of navigation behavior."],[326,"Use `xType=\"time\"` when the X-axis values are Date objects:"],[429,"Use a descriptive group label so removal actions can be announced clearly."],[935,"Use a leading `icon` for recognition, not as the only label - keep a text label."],[1065,"Use a semantic interactive element when possible. For a non-semantic child such as `Avatar` or `Box`, provide an appropriate interactive role and an accessible name. Pressable makes the child focusable when the required props are forwarded."],[423,"Use a string for a simple label. For icons or other composed content, wrap the\nvisible label in `Text` and provide `textValue` for the accessible name. See\n**Toggle Chips** and **Removable Chips** above."],[1227,"Use a text-entry control when exact numeric input is essential. A track is best for exploring or adjusting values within known bounds."],[1216,"Use an array only when every entry has a clear, independently adjustable meaning."],[109,"Use Avatar for informational identity; compose it with `Pressable` for an Avatar Button or Account Menu when it is independently actionable."],[110,"Use circle for people and square for businesses, workspaces, and accounts."],[1173,"Use clear, concise labels"],[383,"Use clear, concise labels that describe what selecting the